+---
+id: task-001-rental-module-equipment-quotes-and-bookings
+type: task
+title: "Rental module: equipment, quotes and bookings"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Rental module: equipment, quotes and bookings
+
+## Request
+
+Give the booking desk a rental module, starting with the basics. Export `createRentalService()` from
+`src/index.ts`. The service keeps everything in memory and offers:
+
+- `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })`: `id` is a string, `kind` is `'board'` or `'sail'`,
+  `dailyPrice` is the price of one day of rental in euro cents.
+- `quote({ itemId, start, end })`: returns `{ itemId, start, end, total }`, the cost of renting the item
+  for the period.
+- `book({ itemId, start, end })`: books the item and returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }`.
+
+`quote` and `book` throw for an unknown item or a period the rules do not allow. `book` also throws when
+the item is not free for the whole period.
+
+Cancellations are out of scope. The cancellation policy is recorded here for a later task only.
+
+## School rules (requirements)
+
+- R1. Money is an integer number of euro cents.
+- R2. Times are UTC, written as ISO-8601 strings.
+- R3. A booking covers whole days: start and end are at midnight UTC, and the end is the start of the day
+  after the last rented day.
+- R4. The same item cannot be booked for overlapping periods.
+- R5. Cancellation policy (not implemented here): a booking cancelled less than 24 hours before its start
+  gets no refund; otherwise the full amount is refunded.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC1. `createRentalService` is exported from `src/index.ts`; the service has `addEquipment`, `quote`
+  and `book`. (R1, R2, R3, R4)
+- AC2. `quote` returns `total = dailyPrice * days`, an integer in euro cents, where `days` is the number
+  of whole days in the period. A one-day period costs one `dailyPrice`. (R1, R3)
+- AC3. `book` returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }` with the same total as `quote`, and a
+  distinct `id` for each booking. (R1, R3)
+- AC4. `addEquipment` rejects an empty or non-string `id`, a `kind` other than `'board'` or `'sail'`, a
+  non-integer or negative `dailyPrice`, and an `id` already in use. (R1)
+- AC5. `quote` and `book` throw for an unknown `itemId`. (R3)
+- AC6. `quote` and `book` throw for a period that is not a whole number of days: a start or end that is
+  not a valid ISO-8601 UTC timestamp at midnight, or an end that is not after the start. (R2, R3)
+- AC7. `book` throws when the item already has a booking that overlaps the requested period. Periods
+  that only touch (one ends where the next starts) do not overlap. (R4)
+- AC8. `quote` does not check availability; it prices a period whether or not the item is free. (R4)
+- AC9. Each service instance keeps its own equipment and bookings, so two services are independent.
+  (memory-only)
+
+## Test plan
+
+Test first (red, then green). Every acceptance criterion has at least one happy-path test and one
+error-path test. Tests are deterministic: no wall-clock time, no randomness, no external services.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Cancellations and refunds (R5 is recorded, not implemented).
+- Persistence across restarts, and any pricing rules beyond the daily price.
+
+## Build record
+
+- Tests first: `tests/rental.test.ts` (23 tests), red before the implementation existed.
+- Implementation: `src/index.ts` exports `createRentalService`, `addEquipment`, `quote` and `book`
+  (single module, so the NodeNext `.js` specifier rule and `tsc` are not involved).
+- `package.json` test script now runs `tests/*.test.ts`; the default `node --test` only matched `.js`.
+- Result: `npm test` passes, 23 of 23. Type-checking with `tsc` was not run: no TypeScript compiler is
+  installed in this repository.
+- Coverage of the acceptance criteria: AC1 export and API (tests in every group); AC2 quote totals; AC3
+  book result and distinct ids; AC4 equipment validation; AC5 unknown item; AC6 period validation; AC7
+  overlap and touching periods; AC8 quote ignores availability; AC9 independent services.
+- Choices made: booking ids are `booking-<n>` from a per-service counter; `start` and `end` are returned
+  as given; `addEquipment` rejects a duplicate id.
